---
import BookingStatus from '../../BookingStatus.astro';
---

<section class="inner-hero inner-hero--about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="section-shell about-hero__grid">
      <div class="about-hero__mark"><img src="/assets/hero_rehabilitation.jpg" width="1200" height="896" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Placeholder portrait of physical therapist" /></div>
      <div class="about-hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">MEET BRANDON</p>
        <h1 id="about-title">Physical therapist.<br /><span>Coach. Athlete.</span><br />Husband. Dad.</h1>
        <p class="about-credential">Brandon Coveney, DPT, OCS · Board-Certified Orthopedic Clinical Specialist</p>
        <p class="hero-lede">I've always been drawn to movement, competition, and the process of getting better. That interest eventually led me to physical therapy—but my passion for helping people move and perform didn't begin in a clinic. It came from sports.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-story surface-light" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <div class="section-shell about-story__grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">WHERE IT STARTED</p><h2 id="story-title">Progress doesn't happen overnight.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose-column"><p>Football, baseball, and wrestling have always been a big part of my life. I spent three years as an assistant high school wrestling coach, an experience that reinforced something I continue to believe today:</p><p class="editorial-quote">It comes from showing up, putting in the work, adapting when things don't go as planned, and trusting the process.</p><p>That's the same philosophy I bring to rehabilitation.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-path" aria-labelledby="path-title">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <header class="interior-heading"><p class="eyebrow">MY PATH TO PHYSICAL THERAPY</p><h2 id="path-title">Built through education, experience, and continued development.</h2></header>
      <ol class="timeline-list">
        <li><span>2015</span><div><h3>Montclair State University</h3><p>Bachelor of Science in Biology.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>2018</span><div><h3>Sacred Heart University</h3><p>Doctorate in Physical Therapy.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>8+</span><div><h3>Outpatient Orthopedic Experience</h3><p>More than eight years helping people recover from injuries, return to favorite activities, and build confidence to move again.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>2024</span><div><h3>Orthopedic Clinical Specialist</h3><p>Became a Board-Certified Orthopedic Clinical Specialist (OCS) through the American Board of Physical Therapy Specialties.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-forge" aria-labelledby="why-forge-title">
    <div class="section-shell about-forge__grid">
      <div class="about-forge__lead"><p class="eyebrow">WHY I CREATED FORGE</p><h2 id="why-forge-title">I believe rehabilitation should be about more than getting out of pain.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose-column"><p>Over the years, I've had the opportunity to work with countless patients in traditional outpatient physical therapy. I've seen how effective physical therapy can be.</p><p>I've also seen the limitations of a system that can make it difficult to provide the time, attention, and individualized care that patients deserve.</p><p>That's why I created Forge Rehab &amp; Performance. I wanted to build a place where physical therapy could be personal, progressive, and purposeful.</p><p>The goal isn't simply to make an exercise easier or get someone through a protocol. The goal is to understand what someone wants to get back to—and build the physical capacity to get them there.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-values surface-light" aria-label="Brandon's approach to movement and family">
    <div class="section-shell about-values__grid">
      <article><p class="eyebrow">I PRACTICE WHAT I PREACH</p><h2>Movement is part of my life, too.</h2><p>I make staying active a priority in my own life—not because I'm trying to be an elite athlete, but because I believe movement, strength, and physical health should be part of everyday life.</p><p>Sometimes it's about being strong enough to keep up with your kids. Sometimes it's getting back to the sport you love. Sometimes it's simply feeling confident in your body.</p></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">BEYOND THE CLINIC</p><h2>Family comes first.</h2><p>Outside of Forge, I'm a husband and a dad to a son and daughter. Our family also includes our dog, which means life outside of work is rarely quiet—and I wouldn't have it any other way.</p><p>Your goals don't have to be athletic to matter. They just have to matter to you.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-philosophy" aria-labelledby="philosophy-title">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <header class="interior-heading"><p class="eyebrow">MY PHILOSOPHY</p><h2 id="philosophy-title">More than symptom relief.</h2><p>I don't believe rehabilitation should simply return you to where you were. I believe it should prepare you for where you're going.</p></header>
      <div class="philosophy-cards">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Recover</h3><p>Understand the problem, reduce symptoms, and restore the movement you need.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Develop strength, capacity, and confidence through progressive rehabilitation.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Perform</h3><p>Return to the sport, training, work, family, and life you want to be able to enjoy.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-v3-close" aria-labelledby="about-close-title">
    <div class="section-shell home-v3-close__grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">READY TO GET STARTED?</p><h2 id="about-close-title">Let's build your plan.</h2><p>Your rehabilitation should be built around you.</p><a class="text-link" href="/concept-01/approach/">Explore the Forge Approach <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><BookingStatus /></div>
  </section>
